WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.980
The next morning a crowd gathered around the statue.

2
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.980
The people had warm clothes and enough food.

3
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:27.959
But many were still complaining about the statue's appearance.

4
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.520
"Our beautiful statue is ugly now!"

5
00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:37.364
"We must catch the thief who stole his gold and jewels!"

6
00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:42.989
"Catch the thief!" people chanted together. "Catch the thief!"

7
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:48.900
The mayor clapped to get everyone's attention.

8
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.330
"Yes, we must catch the thief.

9
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.020
But the king must not see what happened to his beautiful statue."

10
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.620
The mayor drew in a breath. "So we will tear it down!"

11
00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:09.656
"Yes!" the people cheered.

12
00:01:09.657 --> 00:01:15.009
Swallow was too weak and cold to lift his head.

13
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.250
But he could hear everything the people were saying.

14
00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:27.500
He chirped softly. "This statue gave away his beauty to make your lives better!

15
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:34.380
And now you will tear him down? Shame on all of you!"

16
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.180
But of course, reader, the townspeople could not hear Swallow.

17
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.920
Only the statue could hear these words.

18
00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.658
Soon everyone drifted off.

19
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.940
The townspeople were pleased that the bare statue would be torn down.

20
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.720
No longer would it stain their town with its ugliness.

21
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.860
"Thank you for speaking up, Swallow," the statue said.

22
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.840
"But please, save your strength. You need it to get healthy."

23
00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:24.447
Swallow closed his eyes. "I'm afraid that is not my fate, Prince. I—"

24
00:02:24.448 --> 00:02:33.114
Screech! "So it was you who did this to the statue!"

25
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.440
Swallow peeled open his eyes again.

26
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.000
The hungry-looking hawk sat on one of the statue's shoulders!

27
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.500
"You got me at last," Swallow said.

28
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.640
"Yes, I'm the one who took away the statue's beauty.

29
00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:59.220
I'm too weak to fly away now. So go ahead, eat me."

30
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:07.450
"Don't listen to him!" the statue cried. "I asked him to do it!"

31
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:14.600
The hawk eyed the statue. "Why would you do that?"

32
00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.460
"Because from up here I see all the unhappiness in the land.

33
00:03:25.615 --> 00:03:29.364
I had to do something to help people.

34
00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.930
And so, I asked Swallow to help me."

35
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.390
The hawk screeched again. "I cannot believe you did that!"

36
00:03:43.907 --> 00:03:50.639
"Well, I did!" the statue said. "Now leave my dear friend alone.

37
00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:54.570
He is dying, and my heart is breaking.

38
00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.710
Swallow is the best friend I've ever had."

39
00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:08.259
Crack! A loud sound suddenly echoed through the air.

40
00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.370
Startled, the hawk flew off the statue.

41
00:04:12.573 --> 00:04:16.510
With another crack, one of the statue's arms snapped off.

42
00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.430
Then it fell down, sailing toward Swallow!
